{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nFive approved pre-1.0 compatibility commands still invoke their canonical owners. `bridge-status` is the sole hidden alias. The visible aliases are `bridge-fsck`, `bridge-probe`, `jira-onboard`, and `verify-authorship`. Their replacements are `bridge status`, `bridge fsck`, `bridge check-access`, `bridge setup`, and `verify-identity`. `reconcile` plus `reconcile-check` are excluded because their dependency-ordered migration is separate.\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n1. Remove `bridge-status` from `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py:526-535`, `bridge-fsck` from `:536-543`, and `bridge-probe` from `:602-609`. Remove `verify-authorship` factory/handler entries at `:423/:452`. Remove `jira-onboard` factory/handler entries at `:429/:458`. Do not touch `_reconcile`.\n2. Retire alias-only parser, factory, and help wiring. Each old spelling must produce argparse's standard invalid-choice error at parse time with exit code 2. It must not invoke a handler. Each canonical spelling keeps its current owner plus exit behavior.\n3. Regenerate outputs with `scripts/gen_cli_help.py`, `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py`, `scripts/build_cloud_adf_corpus.py`, and `scripts/build_dc_wiki_corpus.py`.\n4. Rebuild the complete test-consumer inventory using a raw string scan for every removed spelling. Retarget behavior-preserving callers to canonical commands. Replace alias-success tests with parser-rejection tests. Remove retired route names from route-census collections.\n5. Replace removed commands in maintained operational prose. Preserve historical ADR plus release-note references as history.\n\n## File Impact\n\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py`, advanced bridge/Jira/verify parser factories, alias help routing — registrations plus alias-only parser wiring\n- `scripts/gen_cli_help.py`, `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py`, `scripts/build_cloud_adf_corpus.py`, `scripts/build_dc_wiki_corpus.py` plus generated help/reference/ADF/wiki outputs\n- maintained CLI, identity, operational docs, `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/release-notes.md` — current versus historical command language\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py`, `test_cli_help_writing_guidelines_jerboa.py`, `test_help_overview_coverage.py`, `test_schema_coverage.py` — generated/documentation contracts\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_status_heldout.py`, `test_bridge_vocabulary.py`, `test_bridge_vocabulary_e2e_heldout.py`, `test_bridge_vocabulary_heldout.py`, `test_intercept_registry_cutover_s6_heldout.py` — bridge command behavior\n- `tests/unit/test_cli_registry.py`, `test_cli_registry_dispatch.py`, `test_jira_onboard.py`, `test_identity_ac7_bff8_heldout.py`, `test_identity_ts3_117b.py`, `test_identity_ts3_117b_heldout.py`, `test_identity_3183.py`, `test_identity_3183_heldout.py`, `test_authorship_batched_ticket_map_7084.py`, `test_reclaim_collapse.py`, `test_enrich_drain.py` — route census, alias-success, subprocess, and canonical migration coverage\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The registry contains no `bridge-status` entry.\n- [ ] The registry contains no `bridge-fsck` entry.\n- [ ] The registry contains no `bridge-probe` entry.\n- [ ] The registry contains no `jira-onboard` entry.\n- [ ] The registry contains no `verify-authorship` entry.\n- [ ] `bridge-status` is treated as the sole hidden alias in migration history.\n- [ ] The other four spellings are treated as visible aliases in migration history.\n- [ ] Each removed spelling produces argparse invalid-choice exit code 2.\n- [ ] No removed spelling reaches its handler.\n- [ ] `bridge status` preserves current owner plus exit behavior.\n- [ ] `bridge fsck` preserves current owner plus exit behavior.\n- [ ] `bridge check-access` preserves current owner plus exit behavior.\n- [ ] `bridge setup` preserves current owner plus exit behavior.\n- [ ] `verify-identity` preserves current owner plus exit behavior.\n- [ ] Each listed bridge vocabulary, generated-help, generated-reference, schema, Cloud ADF, and Data Center wiki artifact is regenerated without a removed command.\n- [ ] Each listed route-census test removes retired names.\n- [ ] Each listed alias-success test is replaced by an invalid-choice assertion.\n- [ ] Each listed subprocess invocation uses a canonical command.\n- [ ] `rg -l -e \"bridge-status\" -e \"bridge-fsck\" -e \"bridge-probe\" -e \"jira-onboard\" -e \"verify-authorship\" tests` is reviewed. Its remaining matches are rejection coverage, generated fixtures, or historical assertions with current behavior moved to canonical commands.\n- [ ] Maintained operational prose uses canonical commands.\n- [ ] Historical ADR plus release references retain old spellings only as historical evidence.\n- [ ] Changelog/release material records each pre-1.0 replacement.\n- [ ] `reconcile` plus `reconcile-check` remain outside this ticket.\n- [ ] Focused CLI and interface tests pass.\n- [ ] Documentation-generation checks pass.\n- [ ] Lint passes.\n- [ ] Typecheck passes."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788371838044013001,"uuid":"cb1c992c-547e-450f-b297-2022a70cabd8"}